ment."},{"insight":"Whether career visibility, recognition, and fairness concerns create a distinct risk for parents using or seeking flexible work.","linked_objectives":["Measure role clarity, growth opportunity, career visibility, and progression concerns among expecting parents and parents of young children.","Measure whether contributions are recognized and whether workplace fairness is perceived, including compensation and treatment of employees using flexibility."],"decision_impact":"Design career-protection, evaluation, promotion, recognition, and fairness safeguards."}],"respondent_segments":[{"key":"expecting_parent","definition":"Currently working in a paid role and expecting a child or planning parental leave.","qualification_rule":"PARENT_STATUS = Expecting a child or planning parental leave","expected_path":"Eligibility and work model, followed by all seven organizational-health sections with expecting-parent-specific sub-items shown where relevant."},{"key":"parent_of_infant","definition":"Currently working in a paid role and caring for a child in the infant age band.","qualification_rule":"PARENT_STATUS = Parent of an infant or young child AND parent-life-stage sub-item = Infant","expected_path":"Eligibility and work model, followed by all seven organizational-health sections with current-child and childcare sub-items shown where relevant."},{"key":"parent_of_older_young_child","definition":"Currently working in a paid role and caring for an older young child within the study definition.","qualification_rule":"PARENT_STATUS = Parent of an infant or young child AND parent-life-stage sub-item = Older young child","expected_path":"Eligibility and work model, followed by all seven organizational-health sections with current-child and childcare sub-items shown where relevant."},{"key":"not_currently_working","definition":"Respondent does not currently work in a paid role.","qualification_rule":"PARENT_STATUS = Not currently working in a paid role","expected_path":"Terminate immediately as ineligible."},{"key":"not_eligible_parent","definition":"Respondent is working but is neither expecting a child, planning parental leave, nor parenting a young child.","qualification_rule":"PARENT_STATUS = None of these","expected_path":"Terminate immediately as ineligible."},{"key":"unsupported_work_model","definition":"Eligible parent whose current work arrangement is outside remote, hybrid, or mainly office-based work.","qualification_rule":"CURRENT_WORK_MODEL = Other arrangement","expected_path":"Terminate immediately as outside the defined work-model audience."}],"questionnaire_sections":[{"key":"overall_engagement","purpose":"Establish parent eligibility, current work model, overall engagement, pride, and retention baseline. Supports objectives 1 and 2.","question_keys":["PARENT_STATUS","CURRENT_WORK_MODEL","ENPS_SCORE","WORKPLACE_PRIDE","RETENTION_INTENT"]},{"key":"role_growth","purpose":"Measure role clarity, growth, career visibility, practical flexibility, pain-point frequency and severity, caregiving context, childcare access, and policy barriers using compact sub-items within the three mandated questions. Supports objectives 2, 3, 7, and 9.","question_keys":["ROLE_CLARITY","GROWTH_OPPORTUNITY","UNSupported_GOALS"]},{"key":"manager_relationship","purpose":"Measure manager effectiveness, psychological safety, comfort requesting flexibility, responses to caregiving needs, and positive manager behaviours through the mandated manager measures. Supports objective 4.","question_keys":["MANAGER_EFFECTIVENESS","SAFETY_COMFORT","MANAGER_STRENGTHS"]},{"key":"team_collaboration","purpose":"Measure belonging, teamwork quality, meeting norms, collaboration friction, and team support for caregiving through the two mandated team measures. Supports objective 5.","question_keys":["TEAM_BELONGING","TEAMWORK_QUALITY"]},{"key":"culture_values","purpose":"Measure value alignment, culture perception, the most urgent cultural change, and bottom-up policy or manager ideas through the mandated culture measures. Supports objectives 6 and 9.","question_keys":["VALUE_ALIGNMENT","CULTURE_WORDS","CULTURE_CHANGE"]},{"key":"wellbeing_workload","purpose":"Measure workload manageability, boundary erosion, care interruptions, productivity barriers, work-life balance, wellbeing, and work-care overlap through compact sub-items within the two mandated measures. Supports objectives 7 and 8.","question_keys":["WORKLOAD_MANAGEABLE","WORKLIFE_BALANCE"]},{"key":"recognition_fairness","purpose":"Measure recognition, fairness, support awareness and usefulness, unmet needs, policy priorities, urgent problem, greatest-impact action, and a concise concrete example through compact sub-items within the two mandated measures. Supports objectives 8 and 9 and closes the survey.","question_keys":["CONTRIBUTION_RECOGNIZED","COMPENSATION_FAIRNESS"]}],"business_rules":[{"id":"BR1","plain_english":"Use PARENT_STATUS as the combined eligibility and parent-life-stage screener. Terminate respondents who are not currently working in a paid role or who are neither expecting a child, planning parental leave, nor parenting a young child."},{"id":"BR2","plain_english":"If CURRENT_WORK_MODEL is Other arrangement, terminate as outside the defined remote, hybrid, or mainly office-based audience."},{"id":"BR3","plain_english":"Show only the pregnancy, leave, return-to-work, childcare, child-age, and care-interruption sub-items relevant to the respondent's PARENT_STATUS and parent-life-stage response; skip irrelevant sub-items without creating additional respondent-facing question keys."},{"id":"BR4","plain_english":"Use ROLE_CLARITY, GROWTH_OPPORTUNITY, and UNSupported_GOALS as compact grids or structured modules to stay within the exact 20-question budget while retaining measures of schedule control, pain-point frequency and severity, career visibility, support gaps, and policy barriers."},{"id":"BR5","plain_english":"Use WORKLOAD_MANAGEABLE and WORKLIFE_BALANCE as compact grids containing boundary erosion, after-hours work, meeting spillover, care interruptions, productivity barriers, wellbeing, and work-care overlap items."},{"id":"BR6","plain_english":"Use CULTURE_CHANGE and the closing recognition/fairness module to capture forced prioritisation, the most urgent problem, greatest-impact employer action, support-policy awareness/access/usefulness, and one bottom-up example."},{"id":"BR7","plain_english":"Ask sensitive workplace and caregiving items using empathetic, no-blame wording and reassure respondents that answers are anonymous and reported in aggregate."},{"id":"BR8","plain_english":"Do not ask age, gender, city, residence, income, NCCS, or other database-known targeting variables; use audience-payload fields for those analyses."},{"id":"BR9","plain_english":"Place behavior and experience measures before evaluations and prioritisation. Use fully labelled five-point scales, limited grids, balanced prioritisation, and targeted open-ended components."},{"id":"BR10","plain_english":"Apply attention checks, speedster detection, straight-line detection, duplicate/inconsistency screening, and open-ended quality review. Quality failures are quality terminates, not ordinary screen-outs."},{"id":"BR11","plain_english":"After respondents complete RECOGNITION_FAIRNESS, including support evaluation, prioritisation, urgent problem, greatest-impact action, and bottom-up example components, complete the survey."}],"dynamic_lists":[],"branch_blocks":[],"termination_and_completion_policy":[{"condition":"PARENT_STATUS indicates that the respondent is not currently working in a paid role.","outcome":"terminate"},{"condition":"PARENT_STATUS indicates None of these: the respondent is neither expecting a child, planning parental leave, nor parenting a young child.","outcome":"terminate"},{"condition":"CURRENT_WORK_MODEL indicates Other arrangement.","outcome":"terminate"},{"condition":"A pregnancy, child-age, childcare, leave, return-to-work, care-interruption, or career-risk sub-item does not apply to the respondent's parent-life-stage or reported experience.","outcome":"skip"},{"condition":"Respondent fails an attention check or quality screen based on speed, straight-lining, duplication, inconsistency, or unusable open-ended content.","outcome":"terminate"},{"condition":"Respondent completes all applicable content through the recognition, support, prioritisation, and decision-close components within RECOGNITION_FAIRNESS.","outcome":"complete"}],"question_generation_instructions":["METHODOLOGY: Employee Engagement — Organizational Health Methodology. Preserve the seven sections and exact order: Overall Engagement, Role & Growth, Manager Relationship, Team & Collaboration, Culture & Values, Wellbeing & Workload, and Recognition & Fairness. Use exactly 20 respondent-facing question keys, with no stimuli or experimental cells.","Use the mandated flow keys exactly as provided. Do not add demographic targeting keys or additional respondent-facing keys.","Use PARENT_STATUS as a combined eligibility and life-stage screener so the exact 20-question budget is maintained. Include expecting-parent, current-parent, not-working, and none-of-these response paths.","Keep the tone empathetic, anonymous, neutral, and no-blame. Avoid leading agree/disagree batteries.","Use compact grids and structured sub-items to capture current/preferred work arrangement, schedule control, childcare access, care interruptions, pain-point frequency and severity, boundary erosion, productivity barriers, career visibility, policy awareness/access/usefulness, and unmet need without adding question keys.","Implement the advanced techniques: include a stay/leave or retention-risk signal through RETENTION_INTENT, a workplace/career risk signal within ROLE_CLARITY or GROWTH_OPPORTUNITY, and a bottom-up policy or manager-behaviour example within CULTURE_CHANGE or the closing recognition/fairness module.","Measure behavior before attitudes, attitudes before prioritisation, and place the most valuable open-ended example late in the questionnaire.","Use fully labelled five-point scales, behavioral anchors, limited grids, forced prioritisation, and concise open-ended probes suitable for an 8–12 minute mobile survey.","Cross-tab results by current work model, parent life stage, caregiving situation, childcare access, and audience-payload age/gender fields without recollecting those database variables.","Complete the survey after the Recognition & Fairness section. Quality failures must be classified separately from ordinary eligibility screen-outs."],"analysis_tags":["eligibility_status","parent_status","parent_life_stage","pregnancy_stage","child_age_group","caregiving_role","childcare_access","care_interruption_frequency","leave_status","current_work_model","preferred_work_model","work_arrangement_gap","office_attendance_predictability","schedule_control","meeting_schedule_control","temporary_schedule_control","workplace_pain_point_frequency","workplace_pain_point_severity","boundary_erosion","productivity_barriers","workload_pressure","manager_effectiveness","flexibility_request_comfort","manager_care_response","psychological_safety","team_support","meeting_norms","career_visibility_risk","promotion_confidence","performance_evaluation_concern","important_work_access","support_awareness","support_access","support_usefulness","support_unmet_need","policy_priority","urgent_problem","greatest_impact_action","workplace_pride","retention_intent","stay_leave_driver","wellbeing_impact","productivity_impact","worklife_balance","culture_perception","bottom_up_idea","open_ended_theme","quality_status"],"assumptions":["PARENT_STATUS will include combined employment eligibility and parent-life-stage options so the binding 20-question budget can be met without adding a separate paid-work screener.","The exact definition and age bands for infant and older young child will be finalised before scripting.","Multi-item grids and sub-items within the mandated flow keys count as one respondent-facing question key.","Age, gender, city, and NCCS are supplied by the audience system and will not be recollected.","The final support-policy and intervention labels will be balanced, concise, and suitable for compact awareness, usefulness, and prioritisation components."],"ambiguities":["The brief does not specify the exact age cut-off for young child or the infant-versus-older-young-child bands.","The brief does not define whether planning parental leave may include caregiving leave unrelated to an expected child; the final PARENT_STATUS options must resolve this.","The fixed 20-question budget requires several objectives to be measured as compact grids or sub-items within the mandated methodology keys rather than as standalone questions."]},"routing_logic":{"text":"{\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"source_business_flow_version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"question_keys\": [\n    {\n      \"key\": \"PARENT_STATUS\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"screener\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"CURRENT_WORK_MODEL\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"screener\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"ENPS_SCORE\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"segment_classifier\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"WORKPLACE_PRIDE\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"segment_classifier\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"RETENTION_INTENT\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"segment_classifier\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"ROLE_CLARITY\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"segment_classifier\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"GROWTH_OPPORTUNITY\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"segment_classifier\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"UNSupported_GOALS\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"branch_followup\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"MANAGER_EFFECTIVENESS\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"segment_classifier\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"SAFETY_COMFORT\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"segment_classifier\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"MANAGER_STRENGTHS\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"branch_followup\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"TEAM_BELONGING\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"segment_classifier\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"TEAMWORK_QUALITY\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"segment_classifier\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"VALUE_ALIGNMENT\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"segment_classifier\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"CULTURE_WORDS\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"branch_followup\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"CULTURE_CHANGE\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"branch_followup\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"WORKLOAD_MANAGEABLE\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"segment_classifier\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"WORKLIFE_BALANCE\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"segment_classifier\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"CONTRIBUTION_RECOGNIZED\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"segment_classifier\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"COMPENSATION_FAIRNESS\",\n      \"expected_role\": \"close\",\n      \"required\": true\n    }\n  ],\n  \"rules\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1\",\n      \"source_question_key\": \"PARENT_STATUS\",\n      \"condition\": {\n        \"operator\": \"equals\",\n        \"values\": [\n          \"Not currently working in a paid role\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"action\": {\n        \"type\": \"terminate\"\n      },\n      \"reason\": \"Terminate immediately because current paid employment is required for eligibility.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2\",\n      \"source_question_key\": \"PARENT_STATUS\",\n      \"condition\": {\n        \"operator\": \"equals\",\n        \"values\": [\n          \"None of these\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"action\": {\n        \"type\": \"terminate\"\n      },\n      \"reason\": \"Terminate immediately because the respondent is neither expecting a child, planning parental leave, nor parenting a young child.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3\",\n      \"source_question_key\": \"CURRENT_WORK_MODEL\",\n      \"condition\": {\n        \"operator\": \"equals\",\n        \"values\": [\n          \"Other arrangement\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"action\": {\n        \"type\": \"terminate\"\n      },\n      \"reason\": \"Terminate because the reported work arrangement is outside the defined remote, hybrid, or mainly office-based audience.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"display_rules\": [],\n  \"dynamic_filters\": [],\n  \"branch_blocks\": [],\n  \"rejoin_rules\": [],\n  \"completion_rules\": [\n    {\n      \"question_key\": \"COMPENSATION_FAIRNESS\",\n      \"condition\": \"always\",\n      \"outcome\": \"complete\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"ambiguities\": [\n    \"The exact qualifying PARENT_STATUS option labels for expecting parents and parents of young children are not fully enumerated; the generated questionnaire must preserve the declared eligibility categories and use stable labels.\",\n    \"Parent-life-stage, pregnancy, childcare, leave, care-interruption, and career-risk sub-items are embedded within the mandated question keys rather than represented as separate flow_keys. Their internal conditional behavior must therefore be implemented inside those question modules, not as additional routing entities.\",\n    \"No flow_key is provided for attention checks, speed detection, straight-line detection, duplication, inconsistency screening, or open-ended quality review. Quality-failure termination cannot be represented as a question-level routing rule without adding an undeclared key.\"\n  ],\n  \"validator_expectations\": [\n    \"All question_keys must exist in generated questions.\",\n    \"No demographic routing is present because the business flow explicitly excludes demographic targeting questions.\",\n    \"PARENT_STATUS and CURRENT_WORK_MODEL are the only eligibility gates declared by the business flow.\",\n    \"Eligible parent-status responses fall through sequentially to CURRENT_WORK_MODEL and then to the shared organizational-health path.\",\n    \"No display_rules are emitted because no separate respondent-facing target question is conditionally excluded; life-stage-specific content is embedded within the mandated compact modules.\",\n    \"No branch_blocks or dynamic_filters are emitted because the business flow declares none.\",\n    \"The final respondent-facing key is COMPENSATION_FAIRNESS, which completes the survey for eligible respondents after all applicable closing-module content is answered.\",\n    \"Quality-failure termination requires a separately declared quality-control flow_key if it must be represented in routing logic.\",\n    \"All rules use flow_key values only and do not use qIds or UUIDs.\"\n  ]\n}","model":"openai.gpt-5.6-luna","sources":[],"data":{"version":"1.0","source_business_flow_version":"1.0","question_keys":[{"key":"PARENT_STATUS","expected_role":"screener","required":true},{"key":"CURRENT_WORK_MODEL","expected_role":"screener","required":true},{"key":"ENPS_SCORE","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"WORKPLACE_PRIDE","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"RETENTION_INTENT","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"ROLE_CLARITY","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"GROWTH_OPPORTUNITY","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"UNSupported_GOALS","expected_role":"branch_followup","required":true},{"key":"MANAGER_EFFECTIVENESS","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"SAFETY_COMFORT","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"MANAGER_STRENGTHS","expected_role":"branch_followup","required":true},{"key":"TEAM_BELONGING","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"TEAMWORK_QUALITY","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"VALUE_ALIGNMENT","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"CULTURE_WORDS","expected_role":"branch_followup","required":true},{"key":"CULTURE_CHANGE","expected_role":"branch_followup","required":true},{"key":"WORKLOAD_MANAGEABLE","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"WORKLIFE_BALANCE","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"CONTRIBUTION_RECOGNIZED","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"COMPENSATION_FAIRNESS","expected_role":"close","required":true}],"rules":[{"id":"R1","source_question_key":"PARENT_STATUS","condition":{"operator":"equals","values":["Not currently working in a paid role"]},"action":{"type":"terminate"},"reason":"Terminate immediately because current paid employment is required for eligibility."},{"id":"R2","source_question_key":"PARENT_STATUS","condition":{"operator":"equals","values":["None of these"]},"action":{"type":"terminate"},"reason":"Terminate immediately because the respondent is neither expecting a child, planning parental leave, nor parenting a young child."},{"id":"R3","source_question_key":"CURRENT_WORK_MODEL","condition":{"operator":"equals","values":["Other arrangement"]},"action":{"type":"terminate"},"reason":"Terminate because the reported work arrangement is outside the defined remote, hybrid, or mainly office-based audience."}],"display_rules":[],"dynamic_filters":[],"branch_blocks":[],"rejoin_rules":[],"completion_rules":[{"question_key":"COMPENSATION_FAIRNESS","condition":"always","outcome":"complete"}],"ambiguities":["The exact qualifying PARENT_STATUS option labels for expecting parents and parents of young children are not fully enumerated; the generated questionnaire must preserve the declared eligibility categories and use stable labels.","Parent-life-stage, pregnancy, childcare, leave, care-interruption, and career-risk sub-items are embedded within the mandated question keys rather than represented as separate flow_keys. Their internal conditional behavior must therefore be implemented inside those question modules, not as additional routing entities.","No flow_key is provided for attention checks, speed detection, straight-line detection, duplication, inconsistency screening, or open-ended quality review. Quality-failure termination cannot be represented as a question-level routing rule without adding an undeclared key."],"validator_expectations":["All question_keys must exist in generated questions.","No demographic routing is present because the business flow explicitly excludes demographic targeting questions.","PARENT_STATUS and CURRENT_WORK_MODEL are the only eligibility gates declared by the business flow.","Eligible parent-status responses fall through sequentially to CURRENT_WORK_MODEL and then to the shared organizational-health path.","No display_rules are emitted because no separate respondent-facing target question is conditionally excluded; life-stage-specific content is embedded within the mandated compact modules.","No branch_blocks or dynamic_filters are emitted because the business flow declares none.","The final respondent-facing key is COMPENSATION_FAIRNESS, which completes the survey for eligible respondents after all applicable closing-module content is answered.","Quality-failure termination requires a separately declared quality-control flow_key if it must be represented in routing logic.","All rules use flow_key values only and do not use qIds or UUIDs."]},"version":"1.0","source_business_flow_version":"1.0","question_keys":[{"key":"PARENT_STATUS","expected_role":"screener","required":true},{"key":"CURRENT_WORK_MODEL","expected_role":"screener","required":true},{"key":"ENPS_SCORE","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"WORKPLACE_PRIDE","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"RETENTION_INTENT","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"ROLE_CLARITY","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"GROWTH_OPPORTUNITY","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"UNSupported_GOALS","expected_role":"branch_followup","required":true},{"key":"MANAGER_EFFECTIVENESS","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"SAFETY_COMFORT","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"MANAGER_STRENGTHS","expected_role":"branch_followup","required":true},{"key":"TEAM_BELONGING","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"TEAMWORK_QUALITY","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"VALUE_ALIGNMENT","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"CULTURE_WORDS","expected_role":"branch_followup","required":true},{"key":"CULTURE_CHANGE","expected_role":"branch_followup","required":true},{"key":"WORKLOAD_MANAGEABLE","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"WORKLIFE_BALANCE","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"CONTRIBUTION_RECOGNIZED","expected_role":"segment_classifier","required":true},{"key":"COMPENSATION_FAIRNESS","expected_role":"close","required":true}],"rules":[{"id":"R1","source_question_key":"PARENT_STATUS","condition":{"operator":"equals","values":["Not currently working in a paid role"]},"action":{"type":"terminate"},"reason":"Terminate immediately because current paid employment is required for eligibility."},{"id":"R2","source_question_key":"PARENT_STATUS","condition":{"operator":"equals","values":["None of these"]},"action":{"type":"terminate"},"reason":"Terminate immediately because the respondent is neither expecting a child, planning parental leave, nor parenting a young child."},{"id":"R3","source_question_key":"CURRENT_WORK_MODEL","condition":{"operator":"equals","values":["Other arrangement"]},"action":{"type":"terminate"},"reason":"Terminate because the reported work arrangement is outside the defined remote, hybrid, or mainly office-based audience."}],"display_rules":[],"dynamic_filters":[],"branch_blocks":[],"rejoin_rules":[],"completion_rules":[{"question_key":"COMPENSATION_FAIRNESS","condition":"always","outcome":"complete"}],"ambiguities":["The exact qualifying PARENT_STATUS option labels for expecting parents and parents of young children are not fully enumerated; the generated questionnaire must preserve the declared eligibility categories and use stable labels.","Parent-life-stage, pregnancy, childcare, leave, care-interruption, and career-risk sub-items are embedded within the mandated question keys rather than represented as separate flow_keys. Their internal conditional behavior must therefore be implemented inside those question modules, not as additional routing entities.","No flow_key is provided for attention checks, speed detection, straight-line detection, duplication, inconsistency screening, or open-ended quality review. Quality-failure termination cannot be represented as a question-level routing rule without adding an undeclared key."],"validator_expectations":["All question_keys must exist in generated questions.","No demographic routing is present because the business flow explicitly excludes demographic targeting questions.","PARENT_STATUS and CURRENT_WORK_MODEL are the only eligibility gates declared by the business flow.","Eligible parent-status responses fall through sequentially to CURRENT_WORK_MODEL and then to the shared organizational-health path.","No display_rules are emitted because no separate respondent-facing target question is conditionally excluded; life-stage-specific content is embedded within the mandated compact modules.","No branch_blocks or dynamic_filters are emitted because the business flow declares none.","The final respondent-facing key is COMPENSATION_FAIRNESS, which completes the survey for eligible respondents after all applicable closing-module content is answered.","Quality-failure termination requires a separately declared quality-control flow_key if it must be represented in routing logic.","All rules use flow_key values only and do not use qIds or UUIDs."]},"route_logs":[],"urls_referred":[]},"require_auth":false}

